Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5871 is to be kept in a standard humanoid containment cell at all times. Once a week, SCP-5871 is to be given a ball of clay to absorb. All personnel are not permitted to mould SCP-5871.

Description:  SCP-5871 is clay, moulded in the shape of a vaguely humanoid entity. SCP-5871 absorbs clay on contact. SCP-5871 lacks a nose, ears and arms. SCP-5871 is sapient and capable of verbal communication, however, SCP-5871 can’t structure sentences properly.

A pink, sphericalSCP-007, however the object is completely submerged with the clay. When asked about this object, SCP-5871 displays extreme discomfort.

Added Description:  As of ██/██/████, SCP-5871-A has displayed properties similar to SCP-357. Personnel dealing with SCP-871 are to be reminded of this.

